menu "LBR cockpit (driver display)"

    config LBR_IO_BATTERY
        string "Slot 'battery' input spec"
        default ""
        help
            Channel: COCKPIT_BATTERY (percent). Typically an 'adc ...' entry
            on an ADC1 pin of the ESP32-C5 (GPIO 1..6). Use measured voltage
            endpoints for percent calibration. Empty = not fitted (or
            simulated with LBR_SENSOR_SIM).
            Syntax: car/components/sensors/include/lbr/sensor_io.h and
            docs/sensors.md. The dashboard warns at 20% and marks 10% or less
            critical. Battery capacity and charging are TBD. The
            cockpit joins the Central's access point
            (CONFIG_LBR_WIFI_SSID / CONFIG_LBR_WIFI_PASSWORD).

endmenu
